course: dictionary
lesson: 4849
title: Hype: big talk and big excitement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hype is lots of excited talk and advertising about something. Adverts, trailers and posts online often use hype to make a new game, toy or trainer sound amazing. «Hype is lots of excitement» is the simple meaning, so ask yourself: is this excitement real, or is it hype?
explain: Hype can also be a verb. When people hype something, they make a big fuss to get others excited, as in: they hyped the new game. You may also hear hype up. «I'm so hyped for the holidays!» means I am very excited. Hyped is slang, so you will hear it with friends more than in school books.
explain: A good question to ask is whether something lives up to the hype. If a film is hyped for months but turns out dull, it did not live up to the hype. Believe the hype only when the evidence shows it is true, not just because lots of people are shouting about it.
fact: Hype means lots of excited talk or advertising.
fact: To hype something means to make a big fuss about it so people get excited.
fact: «I'm so hyped for the holidays!» means I am very excited.
fact: «That song is hype» is slang meaning the song is exciting or great.
fact: Useful phrases: the hype around, believe the hype, live up to the hype, hype up, hype man.
exercise: What does hype mean in «Hype is lots of excitement»? | *Lots of excited talk and advertising | A kind of boring weather | A type of cheap sweet | A small, quiet room
exercise: Priya says, «I'm so hyped for the holidays!» What does hyped mean here? | Very cold | Very late | Very tired | *Very excited
exercise: A game was hyped for months, but it was dull. What does "did not live up to the hype" mean? | It was sold in every shop | *It was not as good as the advertising promised | It had no adverts at all | It was better than everyone expected
test: A shop says «the best toy ever!» What should you do? | *Check the facts before you believe the hype | Believe it straight away with no questions | Tell everyone it is the best | Buy every toy in the shop
test: Which word means to make a big fuss about something to get people excited? | *Hype | Hush | Ignore | Whisper
exam: «Hype is lots of excitement; if 1 person gains £1,000 and 10 people lose £100 each, the losers lost £1,000 in total.» Each of the 10 losers lost £100. How much did they lose in total? | £100 | £10,000 | £10 | *£1,000
